spans.s:
गन्तव्य॑ n. to be gone (n. impers. w. instr. of subj.);
to be walked (a way), to be approached (esp. sex.);
 to be undergone or
begun;
 to be reached, got, acquired;
 to be understood, intelligible.

गन्धर्व॑ m. N. of a genius, connected with Soma and
the Sun;
 w. अपाम् = गर्भ;
 later mostly pl. the heavenly singers.

गान्धर्व॑ f. गा॑न्धर्वी belonging or peculiar to the
Gandharvas, esp. w. विवाह or विधि m. a marriage without any
ceremony;
 m. a singer, pl. N. of a people;
 n. the art of the Gandharvas
i.e. song, music.

गान्धार m. ई f. a prince and princess of the
Gāndhāris;
 m. pl. = seq.

गन्धि a. smelling of, perfumed with;
 having the mere
smell of a thing, being — only by name.

गन्धिक a. smelling of, perfumed with;
 having the mere
smell of a thing, being — only by name.

गन्धिन् a. smelling of, perfumed with;
 having the mere
smell of a thing, being — only by name.
